            <ArticleTitle>Anaesthetic management of an epileptic pregnant woman for trauma surgery--a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>893-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A young epileptic woman with twin pregnancy (IUD) was posted for orthopaedic correction under general anaesthesia on assisted ventilation with laryngeal mask airway (LMA). The present article focuses on anaesthetic concerns in pre-operative preparation and management of such patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
